// Light that runs out, and cells stiff enough that being buried costs something.
//
// The four settings `the_thicket.ron` discovered, lifted out of that scenario so that any world
// can be run under them. Its own header is the argument and should be read before this is used;
// the short version is that **none of them does anything on its own**, which is why they are one
// ruleset rather than four.
//
// `docs/ECONOMY.md` §5 and §9 are why this exists as a named set at all: making light rival is
// the only dial measured so far that changes which strategy wins, and until there was somewhere
// to put it, testing "the whole library under rival light" meant editing every scenario.
//
// The two carbon settings from `the_thicket.ron` are *not* here. Seeding is terrain, not rules —
// a world says how much carbon is in it, and this says what a cell may do with it.
(
    name: "rival light",
    of: "default",
    notes: "the_thicket.ron's economy, available to any world. Measured; see that file.",
    set: {
        // The only shape light rivalry can take on a slide lit from outside the plane: a cell is
        // shaded by what is lying over it. See MetabolicRates::light_occlusion.
        "biology.metabolism.rates.light_occlusion": 128,
        // Without this, occlusion reaches parity and stops: a shaded cell grows less, shrinks,
        // overlaps less and is therefore shaded less. Stiffness closes that loop.
        "biology.metabolism.rates.rigidity_gain": 16384,
    },
)
